{
 "id": "59a05aaf4d2e",
 "task": "When should we schedule maintenance on the charging stations in the Bolzano area to minimise impact on users? Propose concrete weekday/time windows backed by observed usage.",
 "preset": "maintenance",
 "engine": "claude",
 "model": "sonnet",
 "status": "ok",
 "started_at": "2026-11-14T06:37:22.993682+00:00",
 "markdown": "## Answer\nThe quietest Bolzano-wide period is early morning, 05:00–07:00 on Thursday, Tuesday and Friday, with Thursday the lowest at 0.066 occupancy against 0.435 overall [E2]. We recommend scheduling maintenance in those windows, but the evidence is indicative only because each window rests on 4–5 comparable dates [E2].\n\n## Key findings\n- Thu 05:00-07:00 has the lowest Bolzano-wide occupancy at 0.066 (5 comparable dates) [E2].\n- Tue 05:00-07:00 follows at 0.124 and Fri 05:00-07:00 at 0.146, each with 4 comparable dates [E2].\n- The busiest windows to avoid are Wed 20:00-22:00 at 0.72, Sat 21:00-23:00 at 0.654 and Mon 20:00-22:00 at 0.651 [E2].\n- Weekday occupancy is mostly about 0.4–0.66 from 08:00 to 20:00, so daytime work would affect many users [E2].\n- At the highest-occupancy site, BZ_C_RISPARMIO_01 (occupancy 0.669, full_time 0.462, 203 observed starts), even the quietest windows are close to half occupied: Sat 19:00-21:00 at 0.449, Mon 15:00-17:00 at 0.465 and Fri 13:00-15:00 at 0.469 [E3, E4].\n- BZ_BOEHLER_01 has one point with occupancy 0.57 and full_time 0.57, so it is busy more than half the time and needs separate planning [E3].\n- Coverage is low at the top sites: 0.147 for BZ_C_RISPARMIO_01, 0.082 for BZ_P_VITTORIA and 0.227 for BZ_BOEHLER_01 [E5].\n\n## Recommendation\n- Schedule routine area-wide maintenance on Thursday 05:00–07:00 first, with Tuesday and Friday 05:00–07:00 as alternatives [E2].\n- Avoid evenings (20:00–22:00 on Mon and Wed, 21:00–23:00 on Sat) and weekday daytime hours [E2].\n- For BZ_C_RISPARMIO_01 there is no usable overnight evidence, because those hours are mostly null. Check with the operator, or collect more data, before committing to a window. If one is needed now, the lowest observed windows are still only indicative [E4].\n- For BZ_BOEHLER_01, which has a single point, plan the work separately and consider announcing the downtime in advance, since no quiet window is established for it [E3].\n\n## Limitations & unknowns\n- Occupancy comes from status observations only. It is not energy, official sessions, demand or faults [E1].\n- The windows rest on only 4–5 comparable dates each, so treat them as indicative [E2].\n- The Bolzano-wide grid has 44 cells below the minimum of 4 comparable dates. Night cells showing 0.0 or null mean no data and are not evidence of low usage [E2].\n- Gaps over 120 minutes number 437, 757 and 196 at the three top sites respectively, and none of them is stale [E5].\n- 22 sites were excluded from the ranking for having under 24 hours of exposure, and 43 of 51 sites had data in the window [E1, E3].\n- Site-specific quiet windows for BZ_P_VITTORIA were not examined, so that data is unavailable here.\n\n## Sources\n- [E1] dataset_overview — Open Data Hub South Tyrol EChargingPlug status, window 2026-09-19..2026-11-14\n- [E2] hourly_profile(scope=bolzano) — Open Data Hub South Tyrol EChargingPlug status, window 2026-09-19..2026-11-14\n- [E3] rank_sites(metric=occupancy) — Open Data Hub South Tyrol EChargingPlug status, window 2026-09-19..2026-11-14\n- [E4] hourly_profile(scope=Neogy-AMPECO:78226) — Open Data Hub South Tyrol EChargingPlug status, window 2026-09-19..2026-11-14\n- [E5] data_quality(site_ids=3 top sites) — Open Data Hub South Tyrol EChargingPlug status, window 2026-09-19..2026-11-14",
